# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# The root .gitignore covers `git push` deploys. This file covers the other
# route: `vercel deploy` from the CLI uploads the directory as it sits on disk,
# and without this it would ship 117 MB of node_modules built on Windows —
# where the executable bit does not survive — giving the build host a vite it
# cannot run:
#     sh: node_modules/.bin/vite: Permission denied
#     Error: Command "npm run build" exited with 126
#
# Vercel installs its own dependencies from package-lock.json, so none of this
# is needed up there.

node_modules
dist
.vite
.vercel

# Secrets. Set VITE_API_BASE_URL in Vercel's Environment Variables instead —
# Vite inlines it at build time, so it has to exist on the build host, not here.
.env
.env.*
